---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Brief = `The computer picks a number between one and a hundred and I
try to find it. Tell me higher or lower each time. When I get
it, tell me how many guesses it took.`;

const SampleOutput = `I'm thinking of a number between 1 and 100.

Your guess: 50 [Enter]
Higher.
Your guess: 75 [Enter]
Lower.
Your guess: 62 [Enter]
Got it! That took 3 guesses.`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-1/cc-set-3" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back to Set 3
        </a>

        <h1>Code Challenge: Guessing Game</h1>

        <h4>
          Difficulty&nbsp;&nbsp;
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="brief">
          <h2>The Brief</h2>

          <Code
            code={Brief}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="What they asked for"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-4">
            <b>Write your requirements list before you write any code.</b> Input,
            calculate, output, and anything you had to decide for yourself. See{" "}
            <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-1/cc-set-3">Set 3</a> for what that looks like.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="notes">
          <h2>Notes</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>You do not know how many guesses it will take, so this is a while loop.</li>
            <li>Counting the guesses means a variable that survives the loop.</li>
            <li>Decide what happens if the player types something that is not a number, and write your decision down.</li>
            <li>Test that guessing the number on the first try reports one guess, not zero.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="sample-output">
          <h2>Sample Output</h2>

          <Code
            code={SampleOutput}
            frame="terminal"
            title="Sample Output"
            lang="txt"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-3">Play it three times. If the answer is the same every time, your random number is outside the loop when it should be, or your comparison is wrong.</p>

          <p class="mt-3">
            <b>Optional, and easier after Activity 1.21.</b> Put{" "}
            <code>confirm("Play again?")</code> around the whole game so those
            three plays happen in one run. Be aware of what you are building: a
            loop containing a loop. <b>The new random number has to be picked
            inside the outer loop</b> &mdash; if it sits above it, every game has
            the same answer, which is the exact bug the paragraph above tells you
            to watch for.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Your requirements list and your program file, named{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">cc-guessing-game</b>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
